390 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This publication began with a simple act of collecting\072 photographing the circles that appear across New York City\056 What started as a study of wheels on cars\054 bikes\054 carts and suitcases grew into a broader search for the circle as a recurring form\054 from manhole covers and traffic mirrors to synagogue windows\054 Bethesda Fountain\054 the Unisphere and the Guggenheim\056 Combining ground\055level photography with aerial views from Google Maps and research into symbolic motifs like the wheel of life\054 the evil eye and astrology charts\054 the project divides its findings into two sides\072 the functional circle\054 round because it has to be\054 and the symbolic circle\054 round because of what it means\056)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 391 0 R
     /Pg 376 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

